  "body": "### Summary\n\nLOT-087 (#179: message actions menu and typed JS bridge) is ready and may start before capture #273 lands (operator decision, 2026-10-29). Every edit link in the corpus comes from a private conversation. So the menu's rules for one's own post on a **public** topic follow legacy and LOT-031 until #273 shows that toolbar. When #273 lands, this review checks the merged lot against it and fixes any difference.\n\n### Scope\n\n- **What #273 settles for LOT-087:**\n  - the shape of the edit link on one's own post in a public topic;\n  - which of the MP, favourite (`addflag`) and alert (`modo.php`) actions remain on that post.\n\n  The pure menu policy (own post, logged out, MP, locked) depends on both.\n- Add a policy test on the new fixture, through LOT-031's parser.\n- If the capture contradicts the policy, fix the policy.\n- Update the LOT-087 and LOT-031 specs (\"Pending capture\") and HFR-PROTOCOL §6c.\n- If the capture confirms the policy, close this issue with a comment naming the fixture and the test.\n\n### Protocol for whoever claims LOT-087\n\nThe lot's agent tries to do the capture. It comments here once, from the lot's session:\n- **If it is a CLI session with capture access** (the maintainer's Mac, LOT-001 kit): it does #273 first (a read-only GET of a page that already holds a post of the account), then names the capture PR and the fixture id.\n- **Otherwise:** it states:\n  - what the policy assumes for one's own post on a public topic, with the legacy file:line (`MessagePopupMenuPolicy`, `ObjCMessageActionsBuilder.m`);\n  - where the spec lists the pending capture;\n  - the lot's PR.\n\n### Depends on\n\n- #273 (capture)\n- LOT-087 (#179) merged\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A test of the menu policy runs on the #273 fixture (own post, public topic) and passes. It is shown to fail if an action the capture shows is dropped, or if one it does not show is added.\n- [ ] The \"Pending capture\" item is removed from the LOT-087 and LOT-031 specs (or rewritten with what remains), and HFR-PROTOCOL §6c records the verified fact.\n- [ ] If the user-visible behaviour changes, `docs/CHANGELOG-LEGACY.md` has a row for it.\n- [ ] The PR says `Closes #<this issue>` and `Refs #179`.\n\n### Model\n\nFable reviews, or any model other than LOT-087's author model (AGENTS.md §6; LOT-087 is routed Opus → Fable).",
